Srinagar. Weavers work from a coded pattern called a talim, a script that has been passed down for generations and can only be read by those trained in it.","Deep burgundy is the traditional ground for bridal kani, offset here with an antique gold pallav at either end."],"gender":"women","categorySlug":"womens-shawls","collectionSlugs":["womens-shawls","womens-pashmina","pashmina","kashmiri-collection","wedding-collection","luxury-collection","heritage-collection"],"material":"Pure Pashmina","materialSlug":"pure-pashmina","pattern":"Kani Weave","patternSlug":"kani","craft":"Hand-woven kani technique from a talim pattern script","price":47999,"compareAtPrice":59999,"currency":"INR","images":[{"url":"/images/products/burgundy-kani-weave-pashmina-shawl-1.png","alt":"Pashmore women's burgundy kani weave pashmina shawl in burgundy, photographed flat to show the full drape","width":800,"height":1000,"isPrimary":true},{"url":"/images/products/burgundy-kani-weave-pashmina-shawl-2.png","alt":"Pashmore women's burgundy kani weave pashmina shawl in burgundy, detail view of the hand-finished border","width":800,"height":1000,"isPrimary":false},{"url":"/images/products/burgundy-kani-weave-pashmina-shawl-3.png","alt":"Pashmore women's burgundy kani weave pashmina shawl in burgundy, macro close-up of the woven texture","width":800,"height":1000,"isPrimary":false},{"url":"/images/products/burgundy-kani-weave-pashmina-shawl-4.png","alt":"Pashmore women's burgundy kani weave pashmina shawl in burgundy, styled over the shoulder on model","width":800,"height":1000,"isPrimary":false}],"colors":[{"name":"Burgundy","slug":"burgundy","hex":"#5C2233"},{"name":"Crimson","slug":"crimson","hex":"#83282E"}],"sizes":["$21:0:props:recommendations:2:sizes:0"],"variants":[{"id":"burgundy-kani-weave-pashmina-shawl-burgundy-shawl-110x220","sku":"PSH-BURGUN-BUR-01","colorSlug":"burgundy","sizeSlug":"shawl-110x220","price":47999,"compareAtPrice":59999,"inventory":2},{"id":"burgundy-kani-weave-pashmina-shawl-crimson-shawl-110x220","sku":"PSH-BURGUN-CRI-02","colorSlug":"crimson","sizeSlug":"shawl-110x220","price":47999,"compareAtPrice":59999,"inventory":0}],"inventory":2,"badges":["exclusive","handcrafted","limited"],"specifications":[{"label":"Material","value":"Pure Pashmina"},{"label":"Weave / Craft","value":"Hand-woven kani technique from a talim pattern script"},{"label":"Pattern","value":"Kani Weave"},{"label":"Dimensions","value":"110 × 220 cm"},{"label":"Weight","value":"250 g"},{"label":"Finish","value":"Hand-rolled edge with gold pallav"},{"label":"Country of Origin","value":"India"}],"careInstructions":"$21:0:props:recommendations:0:careInstructions","countryOfOrigin":"India","publishedAt":"2026-02-14","popularity":90,"faqs":[{"question":"Is the Burgundy Kani Weave Pashmina Shawl handmade?","answer":"Yes. Every Pashmore piece is hand-spun, handwoven and hand-finished by artisan families in Kashmir. Small irregularities in the weave are the signature of handwork, not a defect."},{"question":"How do I know the Pashmina is genuine?","answer":"Each order ships with a craft certificate recording the fibre grade, the loom it was woven on and the name of the weaver who finished it."},{"question":"Can I return it if the colour is not what I expected?","answer":"Yes. Unused pieces in their original packaging can be returned within 14 days of delivery. Handwoven textiles photograph slightly differently under different light, so we make returns straightforward."}],"rating":{"average":5,"count":18},"relatedSlugs":"$undefined"},"sizes":"(min-width: 1280px) 22vw, (min-width: 768px) 30vw, 45vw","priority":true}],"$L30","$L31","$L32","$L33"]}]]}]
2a:["$","section",null,{"className":"border-t border-line bg-cream/40 py-20","children":["$","div",null,{"className":"container-luxe max-w-3xl","children":[["$","article","The four crafts",{"className":"mt-14 first:mt-0","children":[["$","h2",null,{"className":"font-serif text-[1.75rem] leading-tight text-charcoal md:text-[2.25rem]","children":"The four crafts"}],[["$","p","Kani is woven: the pattern is co",{"className":"mt-5 text-[0.9375rem] leading-relaxed text-mocha","children":"Kani is woven: the pattern is constructed thread by thread using dozens of small wooden bobbins, following a coded script called a talim. It is the slowest and rarest of the four."}],["$","p","Sozni is embroidered with a sing",{"className":"mt-5 text-[0.9375rem] leading-relaxed text-mocha","children":"Sozni is embroidered with a single needle in fine silk thread, worked so precisely that the reverse of the shawl is nearly as clean as the face. Tilla uses flattened metallic thread couched onto the surface, traditionally for occasion and bridal pieces. Jamawar covers the whole ground with woven pattern rather than confining it to a border."}]],"$undefined"]}],["$","article","How long each takes",{"className":"mt-14 first:mt-0","children":[["$","h2",null,{"className":"font-serif text-[1.75rem] leading-tight text-charcoal md:text-[2.25rem]","children":"How long each takes"}],[["$","p","Time on the piece is the honest ",{"className":"mt-5 text-[0.9375rem] leading-relaxed text-mocha","children":"Time on the piece is the honest measure of a Kashmiri shawl’s value."}]],["$","ul",null,{"className":"mt-6 flex flex-col gap-2.5","children":[["$","li","Plain handloom shawl: 4–6 weeks on the loom",{"className":"flex items-start gap-3 text-[0.9375rem] text-mocha","children":[["$","span",null,{"aria-hidden":true,"className":"mt-2.5 h-px w-3 shrink-0 bg-gold"}],"Plain handloom shawl: 4–6 weeks on the loom"]}],["$","li","Border sozni: 3–6 months of needlework",{"className":"flex items-start gap-3 text-[0.9375rem] text-mocha","children":[["$","span",null,{"aria-hidden":true,"className":"mt-2.5 h-px w-3 shrink-0 bg-gold"}],"Border sozni: 3–6 months of needlework"]}],["$","li","Full sozni: 12–24 months",{"className":"flex items-start gap-3 text-[0.9375rem] text-mocha","children":[["$","span",null,{"aria-hidden":true,"className":"mt-2.5 h-px w-3 shrink-0 bg-gold"}],"Full sozni: 12–24 months"]}],["$","li","Jamawar: 3–8 months, depending on colour count",{"className":"flex items-start gap-3 text-[0.9375rem] text-mocha","children":[["$","span",null,{"aria-hidden":true,"className":"mt-2.5 h-px w-3 shrink-0 bg-gold"}],"Jamawar: 3–8 months, depending on colour count"]}],["$","li","Full-field kani: up to 2 years for two weavers",{"className":"flex items-start gap-3 text-[0.9375rem] text-mocha","children":[["$","span",null,{"aria-hidden":true,"className":"mt-2.5 h-px w-3 shrink-0 bg-gold"}],"Full-field kani: up to 2 years for two weavers"]}]]}]]}],["$","article","Buying with confidence",{"className":"mt-14 first:mt-0","children":[["$","h2",null,{"className":"font-serif text-[1.75rem] leading-tight text-charcoal md:text-[2.25rem]","children":"Buying with confidence"}],[["$","p","Turn every piece over. Real sozn",{"className":"mt-5 text-[0.9375rem] leading-relaxed text-mocha","children":"Turn every piece over. Real sozni is clean on the reverse; a true kani shows the pattern mirrored with short floating ends where colours change; printed imitations are flat and uniform on the back."}],["$","p","Every Pashmore piece ships with ",{"className":"mt-5 text-[0.9375rem] leading-relaxed text-mocha","children":"Every Pashmore piece ships with a certificate recording the technique, the fibre grade, the loom and the name of the artisan who finished it."}]],"$undefined"]}]]}]}]
2b:["$","section",null,{"className":"border-t border-line py-20","aria-labelledby":"landing-faqs","children":["$","div",null,{"className":"container-luxe max-w-3xl","children":[["$","h2",null,{"id":"landing-faqs","className":"font-serif text-[1.75rem] leading-tight text-charcoal md:text-[2.25rem]","children":"Frequently Asked Questions"}],["$","$L34",null,{"type":"single","collapsible":true,"className":"mt-8","children":[["$","$L35","What is the difference between kani and sozni?",{"value":"faq-0","children":[["$","$L36",null,{"children":"What is the difference between kani and sozni?"}],["$","$L37",null,{"children":"Kani is a weaving technique — the pattern is built into the cloth on the loom using small wooden bobbins. Sozni is embroidery worked with a needle onto cloth that is already woven. Kani is generally rarer and slower."}]]}],["$","$L35","Are Kashmiri shawls always Pashmina?",{"value":"faq-1","children":[["$","$L36",null,{"children":"Are Kashmiri shawls always Pashmina?"}],["$","$L37",null,{"children":"No. Kashmiri workshops weave Pashmina, fine merino and heavier handloom wool. The craft describes where and how it was made; Pashmina describes the fibre."}]]}],["$","$L35","What is a talim?",{"value":"faq-2","children":[["$","$L36",null,{"children":"What is a talim?"}],["$","$L37",null,{"children":"A coded pattern script used in kani weaving, in which each symbol represents a colour and a number of warp threads. It is read aloud in the workshop and can only be interpreted by someone trained in the notation."}]]}]]}]]}]}]
